00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.000
let's start with how spf testing is done
i have another video that goes into a&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.280
lot more detail about what spf means
and i'd recommend that you watch that&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.000
video first in short spf measures how
much protection you get from erythemal&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.160
or sunburn causing uv from a sunscreen
or any other product&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.000
spf tests are done by putting two
milligrams per square centimeter of&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.080
sunscreen on the backs of human
volunteers a special uv lamp is shone&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.040
onto the backs
and they compare how much uv the skin&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.720
can take with or without the sunscreen
there are a lot of really annoying&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.000
things about this test
anything that involves human volunteers&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.120
is a lot more expensive than if you just
have to use a machine&nbsp;

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.800
it's five to ten thousand us dollars for
a test and if the first version of your&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.120
sunscreen doesn't give you a high enough
spf&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.240
then you have to repeat this again and
again until you get it and&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.800
you are harming people with this test so
the sun care industry has been working&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.480
for a long time to find an alternative
way of testing spf&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.640
but the main issue that keeps coming up
is that it is really hard to mimic how&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.800
sunscreen reacts with human skin
human skin is bumpy and so if you have a&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.320
thicker sunscreen then some of it might
not get into the grooves&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.800
and you might have little bits of hills
sticking up sunscreens also dry on skin&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.160
in a particular way which might be
different from drying on glass or on&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.680
different types of plastic
so the international standard test for&nbsp;

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.760
spf labeling the iso 24444 test
and the fda test which is very similar&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.600
both of these still use in vivo tests on
actual human beings&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.160
this applies to most places worldwide
including the us korea and australia&nbsp;

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.040
there are little differences between the
regions with things like how&nbsp;

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.720
reproducible the test is
and how many volunteers you have to use&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.840
but in essence the test is the same
[Music]&nbsp;

