the saying that the ingredients list&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.640
can't tell you the whole story about how
a product works&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.880
is especially applicable to sunscreens
cosmetic formulators know this really&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:37.440
well
because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.480
sunscreens are one of the
hardest things to formulate&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.240
it can take months to finish a sunscreen
one cosmetic chemist told me that she&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.360
just finished formulating a sunscreen
and it took her six months&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.840
and she started with an spf 30 base and
she just had to raise the spf&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.840
so obviously protection isn't just about
the amounts of filters you put into it&nbsp;

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.480
because if it was then they'd be done in
